comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T06:14:40.384Z","harness:claude-code","Still live at HEAD 2026.7.31, verified 2026-07-31. `pm next --for execute` emits budget_exceeded.omitted_result: true alongside within_budget: true in one envelope, with token_budget 1200 and estimated_tokens 79 — the receipt reports the omitted-result payload as within budget, so the two keys in the same envelope assert opposite things. The recovery instruction \"Repeat the original command without --for\" costs 9,259 bytes against the 320-byte refusal."
  "2026-08-01T00:37:52.411Z","harness:codex","Delivery evidence 2026-08-01: receipts now distinguish declaration_feasible and result_omitted, omitted results always report within_budget:false, recovery never recommends an unprojected retry, and deterministic string then row compaction retains useful rows before receipt-only fallback. The checked 27-item fixture and all five live 2243-item tracker probes deliver feasible results; an explicit 256-token control proves truthful omission. Remaining acceptance before closure: publish and gate the required two-item versus current-scale calibration table rather than relying on the current small committed fixture plus manual live evidence."
  "2026-08-01T01:34:18.884Z","harness:codex","PR #849 review evidence: list/get/search now reject tokenBudget without a selected intent while context/next retain their established standalone budget semantics; 2,000-row compaction uses batch estimation and completed with fewer than 20 JSON serializations; duplicate terminal estimation was removed; generated schemas now use generic wording except the deps-scoped override. Focused regression tests passed 111/111 after narrowing the validation, and the repo-wide suite passed 6636/6636 at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. Remaining original closure acceptance is unchanged: the current-scale calibration table and mandatory gate are still outstanding, so this item returns to open."
  "2026-08-01T01:45:28.140Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence: exact token budgets now normalize token_budget to tokenBudget, reject ambiguous get/list/search usage without --for while preserving context/next standalone behavior, and use truthful budget-derived search guidance. The release gate independently measures serialized stdout, requires finite numeric receipt fields, and rejects actual output above the declared receipt budget. Focused review tests and the complete sandboxed coverage suite pass; latest full result is 6637/6637 tests with 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines. Remaining current-scale calibration-table acceptance stays open and is not claimed as delivered."
  "2026-08-01T01:56:15.853Z","harness:codex","Exact local release-gate evidence before the review-fix push: static quality and 100% docstring gates passed; package boundary, SDK contract parity, 28-surface token budget, gate registry, SDK surface, benchmarks, context/retrieval evaluations, and the 96-surface agent-token gate passed; 410 files and 6637 tests passed at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage; secret scan, packed npx smoke, and the 88-command isolated package-first dogfood run passed. The only terminal release:gates failure was the hosted Greptile adapter reporting free_reviews_limit_reached after all local gates completed; this is external review capacity, not a product/test failure."
  "2026-08-01T02:04:45.101Z","harness:codex","Exact-head CI static correction: the structured missing_required_option path added in sdk/context-intent-contracts.ts is now present in the generated error-code catalog and full contracts fixture. pnpm contracts:check, security:scan, lint, and the focused generator/context tests pass. This fixes the only Actions failure on 6b0e063d5; the original current-scale calibration acceptance remains open."
  "2026-08-01T05:27:13.441Z","harness:codex","Calibration evidence 2026-08-01: reproducible seed 42 runs both a two-item workspace and the current 2,243-item scale across context/get/list/next/search. Small-tier measured tokens are 707,401,393,395,301; scale-tier measured tokens are 1000,415,3181,1171,1763. The executable gate and exhaustive negative-path tests are registered in quality:static and pass."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-30T17:21:51.507Z","harness:claude-code","Method that found this, reusable for any declared bound: run the identical invocation against a two-item workspace and against the real tracker, and diff the verdicts rather than the outputs. A bound that is satisfied on the small corpus and violated on the large one is a scalar that should have been a function, and the small corpus is the one the number was authored against. A bound violated on both is an ordinary miscalibration. A bound satisfied on both is genuinely scale-invariant and can be left alone.\n\nSecond technique, for the same class: a floor is invisible from the default. Raising the ceiling in steps until content first appears is the only way to measure the smallest form a command can emit, because at the default the response contains no rows to measure. next execute yielded nothing at 1200 and 2000 and content at 4000, which located the floor between 2000 and 4000 and then exactly at 1438 from the receipt. Doing this in the other direction, lowering a working ceiling until output disappears, gives the same number and is cheaper when the default already works."
